<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="git-addon-customizing-ai-support">
  <title>Customize AI Positron Support</title>
  <shortdesc>Provide additional instructions for responses generated by AI models and limit the
    context sent to them.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>AI preferences</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>commit message generation</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>Explain commit</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <taskbody>
    <context>
      <p><ph keyref="product"/> Git Client lets you configure the following AI settings:</p><ul
          id="ul_xgy_bjx_njc">
          <li>Instructions for generated commit messages, commit explanations, and conflict
            resolution explanations</li>
          <li>Maximum characters and commits sent to an AI model as style context</li>
        </ul><note conkeyref="reusables-addons/important_requires_positron"
        id="note_k22_q1b_4jc"/><p>To configure AI support settings, follow these
      steps:</p></context>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Open the <uicontrol conkeyref="sa-preferences/prefs"/> menu and go to <menucascade>
            <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/preferences-plugins"
              >Plugins</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client">Git
              Client</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-ai"
              >AI</uicontrol>
          </menucascade>.</cmd>
        <info><ol id="ol_wt3_45x_njc">
            <li>To open the <uicontrol conkeyref="sa-preferences/prefs"/> menu, on the toolbar, go
              to <menucascade>
                <uicontrol conkeyref="sa-toolbar/sa-toolbar-options"/>
                <uicontrol conkeyref="sa-preferences/prefs"/>
              </menucascade> or <menucascade>
                <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/sa-toolbar-git.dita#sa-toolbar-git/sa-toolbar-git"/>
                <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/sa-toolbar-git.dita#sa-toolbar-git/sa-toolbar-git-settings"/>
                <uicontrol conkeyref="sa-preferences/prefs"/>   
              </menucascade></li>
            <li>On the left sidebar, go to <menucascade>
                <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/preferences-plugins"
                  >Plugins</uicontrol>
                <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client">Git
                  Client</uicontrol>
                <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-ai"
                  >AI</uicontrol>
              </menucascade>, and the <ph keyref="plugin-git-client"/> AI preferences page
                  opens.<p><fig id="fig_bx2_4mk_mjc">
                  <title>Navigating to the <ph keyref="plugin-git-client"/>
                    <uicontrol
                      conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-ai"/>
                    preferences page</title>
                  <image href="../gif/preferences-plugins-git-client-ai.gif" id="image_gsh_pqk_mjc"
                  />
                </fig></p></li>
          </ol></info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Customize AI integration in the <ph keyref="plugin-git-client"/></cmd>
        <info><ol id="ol_az3_wwx_njc">
            <li>To configure the responses generated by AI actions, provide instructions for
              AI-generated responses in a setting's <uicontrol
                conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-additional-instructions"
              /> box. <p><xref href="#./table_pk4_cyx_njd"/> shows what each setting's <uicontrol
                  conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-additional-instructions"
                /> change.</p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_pk4_cyx_njd">
                <title>Configure AI-generated responses</title>
                <tgroup cols="2">
                  <colspec colnum="1" colname="c1" colwidth="1*"/>
                  <colspec colnum="2" colname="c2" colwidth="1*"/>
                  <thead>
                    <row>
                      <entry>Setting</entry>
                      <entry>Changes</entry>
                    </row>
                  </thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <row>
                      <entry><uicontrol
                          conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-commit-message-generation"
                        /></entry>
                      <entry>Commit messages generated by <xref
                          href="git-addon-committing.dita#git-addon-committing/li_git_commit_generate_ai"
                            ><uicontrol
                            conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/git-client-commit-msg-generate-commit-message-using-ai"
                          /></xref>.</entry>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                      <entry><uicontrol
                          conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-explain-commits"
                        /></entry>
                      <entry>Commit explanations generated by <xref
                          href="git-addon-explaining-commits-with-ai.dita#git-addon-explaining-commits-with-ai"
                            ><uicontrol
                            conref="git-history-view.dita#git-history-view/git-history-commit-explain-commit-with-ai"
                          /></xref>.</entry>
                    </row>
                    <row>
                      <entry><uicontrol
                          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/git-client-conflicts-ai-conflict-resolution"
                        /></entry>
                      <entry>Conflict resolution explanations generated by <xref
                          href="git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution.dita#git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution"
                            ><uicontrol
                            conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/git-client-conflicts-resolve-with-ai"
                          /></xref>. </entry>
                    </row>
                  </tbody>
                </tgroup>
              </table></li>
            <li>Adjust the amount of context sent to AI models on <uicontrol
                conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-context"/>.<ul
                id="ul_wvj_1fy_njc">
                <li><uicontrol
                    conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-context-max-chars"
                  />: the maximum number of characters sent to an AI model as prompt context
                  (default is 2,095,152). </li>
                <li><uicontrol
                    conref="../add-ons/plugin-preferences.dita#plugin-preferences/prefs-git-client-context-commits"
                  />: the number of commits sent to an AI model as prompt context (default is
                      5)<p><fig id="fig_tx5_y5n_ljc">
                      <title>Git Client AI preferences</title>
                      <image href="img/preferences/ai_preferences.png"
                        id="image_jrh_bvn_ljc"/>
                    </fig></p></li>
              </ul></li>
          </ol></info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Select <uicontrol>OK</uicontrol> or <uicontrol>Apply</uicontrol> to save your settings.
        </cmd>
      </step>
    </steps>
    <postreq>
      <p>You can save these settings in an <ph keyref="product"/> project file so the same AI guidance
        is shared across a team. When generating a commit message, the AI can also take into account
        the current branch name, recent commit messages, and any draft text already entered in the
        <uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol> field.</p>
    </postreq>
  </taskbody>
</task>
